From: Eden port <editors@example.org>
Subject: [PATCH] doas: Use char ** for environ

musl declares environ as char **; a conflicting const declaration is an
error under modern clang.
---
 usr.bin/doas/env.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/usr.bin/doas/env.c b/usr.bin/doas/env.c
--- a/usr.bin/doas/env.c
+++ b/usr.bin/doas/env.c
@@ -110,7 +110,7 @@
 	fillenv(env, copyset);
 
 	if (rule->options & KEEPENV) {
-		extern const char **environ;
+		extern char **environ;
 
 		for (i = 0; environ[i] != NULL; i++) {
 			struct envnode *node;
